URGENT
Hello,
I write to confirm that I have made an urgent application for a stay of pro=
ceedings, as set out in my application. Please can a District Judge urgentl=
y stay the 9th of February 2026 hearing before the time comes.
I will be away from home for the next few days but remain contactable by em=
ail and telephone.
I intend to appeal matters arising from the hearing on 7 January 2026. In l=
ight of that application and the pending appeal, I will not be attending th=
e hearing listed for 9 February 2026. I have not been given a chance to und=
erstand the hearing at all. It was listed only 33 days after January hearin=
g. Proceeding with this hearing under these circumstances infringes my righ=
ts under Article 6 of the European Convention on Human Rights, which guaran=
tees the right to a fair trial, including the ability to participate effect=
ively in proceedings and to have adequate time and facilities to prepare a =
defence. It also engages my common law rights to natural justice, including=
 the principles of audi alteram partem (the right to be heard) and nemo jud=
ex in causa sua (the right to an impartial tribunal).
Given the lack of opportunity to understand the hearing, the late listing, =
and procedural irregularities at the prior hearing, it would be fundamental=
ly unfair and contrary to these rights to require my attendance. I am justi=
fied in seeking a stay and a hearing before a different Judge to ensure tha=
t the proceedings are conducted fairly and without any real or perceived bi=
as.
Meanwhile, my N244 application in relation to my case against Mr McGhee has=
 not yet been acknowledged by any court, including the Manchester Civil Cou=
rt. I am also yet to receive an update on the defendant=92s application reg=
arding the case against Ms Soul to set aside her County Court judgment, whi=
ch was submitted in September. Attempting to combine these cases while such=
 outstanding matters remain unresolved is procedurally improper and reflect=
s poor case management by Judge Geddes.
I respectfully maintain that the manner in which the hearing on 7 January 2=
026 was conducted was procedurally unfair. I raised objections during the h=
earing and sought to resist the approach taken. I am currently considering =
my further options in relation to appeal and related procedural remedies.
I trust the Court will deal with the urgent application accordingly.

Kind regards,
Abdul Alim
